# Markdown belongs to markdownlint, not Prettier.
#
# Prettier rewrites *emphasis* to _emphasis_ and there is NO option to stop it: on 3.9.5,
# `getSupportInfo()` reports zero options applicable to the markdown parser (only --prose-wrap,
# which is about wrapping). Upstream has declined to make the marker configurable.
#
# That rewrite is not cosmetic here. A Python file named *file*.py becomes _file_.py — which
# CommonMark parses as emphasis (a `_` may close before punctuation), so the page renders a
# silently italicised "file.py" and the real name is lost. Backticked spans are safe; running
# prose is not.
#
# The house style (asterisks, see .claude/skills/markdown-style) is now enforced mechanically
# by MD049/MD050 in .config/.markdownlint.json instead of being contradicted here.
*.md
*.mdx
